          "explanation": "<p>Given:</p>\n\n<p>Eight people:- P, Q, R, S, T, U, V, W. All of them are sitting in a straight line facing north direction.</p>\n\n<p>1) At most three people are sitting to the right side of S.</p>\n\n<p>2) S is not sitting at any of the extreme ends.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/11/F1_Sagar_Shraddha_19.11.2020_D31.png\" style=\"width: 421px; height: 291px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>3) P is sitting at the second to the left of S.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/11/F1_Sagar_Shraddha_19.11.2020_D32.png\" style=\"width: 421px; height: 290px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>4) Q is sitting at one of the extreme ends.</p>\n\n<p>5) T is second to the right of Q.</p>\n\n<p>To make T sit at the right of Q, we have to arrange Q at the left end only. As, if we arrange Q at the right end, we wouldn&#39;t be able to arrange T on the right side of Q.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/11/F1_Sagar_Shraddha_19.11.2020_D33.png\" style=\"width: 421px; height: 291px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>Possibility 3 is cancelled now as in this case, there is no place for T at the second to the left of Q.</p>\n\n<p>6) There are two people sitting between R and U and neither of them is sitting at the extreme ends.</p>\n\n<p>7)&nbsp;U is not the neighbour of T.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/11/F1_Sagar_Shraddha_19.11.2020_D34.png\" style=\"width: 421px; height: 186px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>Possibility 1 is cancelled now as there is no suitable pace left for R and U such that they have 2 people between them.</p>\n\n<p>8)&nbsp;&nbsp;V is neither the neighbour of Q nor sitting at any of the extreme ends.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/20/11/F1_Sagar_Shraddha_19.11.2020_D35.png\" style=\"width: 420px; height: 58px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>Hence,&nbsp;<strong>Q</strong>&nbsp;is sitting fourth to the left of U.</p>",
